{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 1 RCA — CONFIRMED at runtime (rebar-debug)\n\nThe suspicion in the scope note is correct: **this is a wiring job, not new accounting.** The\nloop-vs-breadth signal is already computed on the failure path and then thrown away one frame\nfrom the write.\n\n### Root cause 1 (the \"computed then discarded\" defect)\n\n`usage_log.record()` builds its row from a fixed allowlist,\n`_FIELDS = (input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_tokens, cache_write_tokens, requests)`\n(`src/rebar/llm/usage_log.py:32`), iterated at `usage_log.py:311-312`. Everything else in the\n`usage` dict is silently dropped.\n\n`record_failure()` (`usage_log.py:320`) hands `record()` the FULL `failure_usage()` dict\n(`usage_log.py:136-191`), which computes seven further keys — `tool_calls`,\n`tool_calls_distinct`, `max_consecutive_repeat`, `top_repeated_tool_calls`, `request_limit`,\n`tool_calls_limit`, `finish_reason`. **All seven are discarded at the write.**\n\nThis violates the module's own cited contract twice over:\n- `record_failure`'s docstring (`usage_log.py:338-345`): the failure row \"is deliberately the\n  SAME shape a successful one has ... Counters come from `failure_usage`, which reads what was\n  actually burned\".\n- `failure_usage`'s docstring (`usage_log.py:150-156`) declares the whole POINT of the\n  signature summary: \"a run with many calls but few distinct signatures is looping; one with\n  many distinct signatures is exploring.\"\n\nThe signal survives only as an ephemeral log line via `format_repetition` (`usage_log.py:237`).\n\n**Discriminating experiment (runtime, offline `FunctionModel` exhaustion run through the real\n`PydanticAIRunner`).** Prediction if the root cause is true: `failure_usage()` returns the loop\nsignal and the FILE row lacks it. Observed:\n\n    failure_usage() COMPUTED: requests=125 tool_calls=125 tool_calls_distinct=1\n                              max_consecutive_repeat=125 request_limit=125 tool_calls_limit=250\n                              top_repeated_tool_calls=[{read_file:9148ca16, 125}]\n    ROW WRITTEN TO DISK:      op/outcome/model/timestamp + input/output/cache_read/\n                              cache_write/requests   <- 125 requests, nothing else\n    COMPUTED BUT DISCARDED:   finish_reason, max_consecutive_repeat, request_limit,\n                              tool_calls, tool_calls_distinct, tool_calls_limit,\n                              top_repeated_tool_calls\n\nA textbook 125/1 loop (distinct ratio 0.008) is recorded on disk as indistinguishable from 125\nrequests of genuine breadth. This is the exact class 70bc's windowed distinct-ratio needs and\ncannot get.\n\n### Root cause 2 (why nothing is recorded for a normal gate run)\n\n`record()` no-ops unless `REBAR_USAGE_LOG` names a path (`usage_log.py:295-297`). It is set in\nexactly three places — `prompt-eval.yml`, `external-integration.yml`, and the review-bot\nservice in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:212`. **A local operator gate run sets none of\nthem, so it records nothing at all** — which is precisely why answering one question required\nfour live instrumented runs. Not explainable by root cause 1; a genuinely separate mechanism.\n\n### Root cause 3 (the success path never computes the shape)\n\n`_extract_usage` (`src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:453-484`, re-exported into `runner.py:50`)\nreturns exactly five keys and no `tool_calls`. Verified at runtime: the success row is\n`requests=1` with no tool-call field. Neither row carries wall-clock duration.\n\n### What IS already persisted (so no second mechanism gets built)\n\n- Plan-review sidecar DOES carry per-call `requests` (`plan_review/sizing.py:292-310`) and a\n  `metrics` block with `det_ms`/`llm_ms`/`total_ms`/`llm_calls`\n  (`workflow/plan_review_recovery.py:151-177`). No `tool_calls`.\n- Completion verdict sidecar carries **no** counts, limits or duration at all\n  (`completion_sidecar.py:271-306`).\n- Signed attestations carry no run metadata by design — deliberately timestamp-free so\n  re-signing is reproducible (`_commands/transition_close.py:129-130`).\n- Only `tool_calls` on disk today is the gate-error sidecar, and only on the completion\n  bounded-recovery arm (`workflow/completion_recovery.py:255-267`); the other five\n  `emit_gate_error` sites pass no diagnostic.\n\n### Legitimacy\n\n- RC1: **`defect`** — violates the module's own cited docstring contract (above).\n- RC2/RC3: **`incomplete-implementation`** — cited design authority is\n  `docs/llm-framework.md:698-704`, which gives operators tuning advice (\"a high recursion limit\n  means you're paying for a loop, fix the loop\") premised on data the system never records.\n\nBoth unlock repair.\n\n### Caller-dependency sweep\n\n`record()`'s only callers are `agent_call.record_call_spend` and `usage_log.record_failure`.\nRow consumers (`summarize`, `_read`, `usage_kwargs`) read by `.get(field, 0)` over fixed field\ntuples, so extra keys are ignored — adding keys is backward-compatible for every existing\nreader. No behavioral dependency on the absence of these fields. Clear to proceed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785947291491272001,"uuid":"c1b31ff7-0389-4e0d-97c7-0df945343662"}